"NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027 | NVIDIA Newsroom (https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027)\nciteturn392view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn385view1\",\"pattern\":\"Revenue\"}); Total lines: 462\nL0: PLATFORMS\nL1: \nL2: other links\nL3: \nL4:   * cite0†Developers†developer.nvidia.com L5:   * cite1†Industries†www.nvidia.com L6:   * cite2†Shop†www.nvidia.com L7:   * cite3†Drivers†www.nvidia.com L8:   * cite4†Support†www.nvidia.com L9:   * cite5†About NVIDIA†www.nvidia.com L10: \nL11:   * cite6†View All Products†www.nvidia.com L12:   * cite7†GPU TECHNOLOGY CONFERENCE†www.nvidia.com L13:   * cite8†NVIDIA Blog†blogs.nvidia.com L14:   * cite9†Community†www.nvidia.com L15:   * cite10†Careers†www.nvidia.com L16:   * cite11†TECHNOLOGIES†www.nvidia.com L17: \nL18: cite12†Newsroom L19: \nL20: cite13†NVIDIA in Brief L21: \nL22: cite14†Exec Bios L23: cite8†NVIDIA Blog†blogs.nvidia.com L24: \nL25: cite15†Podcast†blogs.nvidia.com L26: \nL27: cite16†Media Assets L28: \nL29: cite17†In the News L30: \nL31: cite18†Press Contacts L32: \nL33: cite19†Online Press Kits L34: \nL35:   * cite13†NVIDIA in Brief L36:   * cite14†Exec Bios L37:   * cite8†NVIDIA Blog†blogs.nvidia.com L38:   * cite15†Podcast†blogs.nvidia.com L39:   * cite16†Media Assets L40:   * cite17†In the News L41:   * cite18†Press Contacts L42:   * cite19†Online Press Kits L43: \nL44: Press Release\nL45: # NVIDIA Announces Financial Results for Second Quarter Fiscal 2027\nL46: \nL47:   * Revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year ago\nL48:   * Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago\nL49: \nL50: August 26, 2026\nL51: NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago. For the quarter, GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins were both 75.0%. GAAP and non-GAAP earnings per diluted share were $2.46 and $2.22, respectively.\nL52: “AI has reached its inflection point. It’s doing useful work. Its tokens are productive and profitable. Now, compute is revenue,” said Jensen Huang, founder and CEO of NVIDIA. “And demand is accelerating. This time last year, one lab alone was driving the buildout; today, we have a golden age of new AI labs and startups, multiple frontier labs scaling in parallel, a thriving open-model ecosystem and physical AI coming online — with strong momentum across the U.S. and around the world.\nL53: The AI infrastructure buildout is at full steam. Vera Rubin, now in full production, was built to power exactly this moment.”\nL54: During the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA returned approximately $26.0 billion to shareholders in the form of shares repurchased and cash dividends. As of the end of the second quarter, the company had approximately $99.0 billion remaining under its share repurchase authorization.\nL55: \nL56: NVIDIA will pay its next quarterly cash dividend of $0.25 per share on October 1, 2026, to all shareholders of record on September 10, 2026.\nL57: \nL58: Q2 Fiscal 2027 Summary\nL59: GAAP\nL60: ($ in millions, except earnings per share)  | Q2 FY27  | Q1 FY27  | Q2 FY26  | Q/Q  | Y/Y\nL61: Revenue  | $96,221  | $81,615  | $46,743  | 18 %  | 106 %\nL62: Gross margin  | 75.0 %  | 74.9 %  | 72.4 %  | 0.1 pts  | 2.6 pts\nL63: Operating expenses  | $8,408  | $7,621  | $5,413  | 10 %  | 55 %\nL64: Operating income  | $63,734  | $53,536  | $28,440  | 19 %  | 124 %\nL65: Net income  | $59,688  | $58,321  | $26,422  | 2 %  | 126 %\nL66: Diluted earnings per share  | $2.46  | $2.39  | $1.08  | 3 %  | 128 %\nL67: Non-GAAP\nL68: ($ in millions, except earnings per share)  | Q2 FY27  | Q1 FY27  | Q2 FY26  | Q/Q  | Y/Y\nL69: Revenue  | $96,221  | $81,615  | $46,743  | 18 %  | 106 %\nL70: Gross margin  | 75.0 %  | 75.0 %  | 72.5 %  | --  | 2.5 pts\nL71: Operating expenses  | $8,232  | $7,449  | $5,361  | 11 %  | 54 %\nL72: Operating income  | $63,956  | $53,783  | $28,541  | 19 %  | 124 %\nL73: Net income  | $53,954  | $45,548  | $24,763  | 18 %  | 118 %\nL74: Diluted earnings per share  | $2.22  | $1.87  | $1.01  | 19 %  | 120 %\nL75:    |    |    |    |    |\nL76: Outlook\nL77: \nL78: NVIDIA’s outlook for the third quarter of fiscal 2027 is as follows:\nL79: \nL80:   * Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\nL81:   * GAAP and non-GAAP gross margins are expected to be 74.0%, plus or minus 50 basis points.\nL82:   * GAAP and non-GAAP operating expenses are expected to be approximately $9.2 billion and $9.0 billion, respectively.\nL83: For the full year fiscal 2027, NVIDIA expects GAAP and non-GAAP tax rates to be between 16.0% and 18.0%, excluding any discrete items and material changes to NVIDIA’s tax environment.\nL84: \nL85: Highlights\nL86: \nL87: Data Center\nL88:   * Second-quarter revenue was $89.0 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 117% from a year ago.\nL89:   * Announced the cite20†NVIDIA Vera Rubin platform is ramping into full production with racks running at cite21†partners†blogs.nvidia.com including CoreWeave, Google Cloud, Microsoft Azure, Oracle Cloud Infrastructure and Nebius.\nL90:   * Revealed that cite22†NVIDIA Spectrum™-6†blogs.nvidia.com switch systems — supporting both pluggable and co-packaged optics as part of the NVIDIA Vera Rubin platform — are arriving across the world’s gigascale AI factories.\nL91:   * Unveiled cite23†NVIDIA Vera , the first CPU built for AI agents, with broad adoption planned across the world’s leading technology providers.\nL92:   * Announced that cite24†NVIDIA Groq 3 LPX , the interactive AI inference accelerator, is now in full production.\nL93:   * Introduced new security innovations for cite25†NVIDIA Vera BlueField™-4 STX , delivering agentic AI storage processing with in-silicon security for AI factories.\nL94:   * Launched the cite26†NVIDIA DSX™ platform, providing infrastructure builders a complete playbook to design, build and operate AI factories at scale.\nL95:   * Announced strategic partnerships to establish independent cite27†compute financing platforms with Apollo, BlackRock, Blackstone, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs and KKR to mobilize over $500 billion of third-party capital for the buildout of AI infrastructure over time, subject to definitive agreements.\nL96:   * Announced that SpaceXAI will deploy cite28†NVIDIA Vera CPUs to accelerate its next generation of agentic AI applications.\nL108:   * Second-quarter Edge Computing revenue was $7.2 billion, up 13% from the previous quarter and up 27% from a year ago.\nL109:   * Partnered with Microsoft to reinvent the Windows PC with cite45†NVIDIA RTX Spark™ — a 1-petaflop superchip with the full CUDA™ and NVIDIA RTX™ ecosystem.\nL110:   * Announced cite46†NVIDIA DGX Station™ for Windows, the world’s most powerful deskside AI supercomputer for developing and running agents on Windows.\nL139: Revenue  | $  | 96,221  |    | $  | 46,743  |    | $  | 177,837  |    | $  | 90,805\nL140: Cost of revenue  |    | 24,079  |    |    | 12,890  |    |    | 44,538  |    |    | 30,284\nL141: Gross profit  |    | 72,142  |    |    | 33,853  |    |    | 133,299  |    |    | 60,521\nL142:    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |\nL143: Operating expenses  |    |    |    |    |    |    |\nL144:    | Research and development  |    | 7,054  |    |    | 4,291  |    |    | 13,375  |    |    | 8,280\nL269: GAAP cost of revenue  | $  | 24,079  |    |    | $  | 20,458  |    |    | $  | 12,890  |    |    | $  | 44,538  |    |    | $  | 30,284  |\nL270: GAAP gross profit  | $  | 72,142  |    |    | $  | 61,157  |    |    | $  | 33,853  |    |    | $  | 133,299  |    |    | $  | 60,521  |\nL27