Total lines: 754\nNo matching text found for \"Net Debt\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://investor.avinc.com/static-files/2e8254ff-1cc6-4041-bd07-943248b7820d)\nciteturn392view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 29; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn385view3\",\"pattern\":\"capital expenditures\"}); Total lines: 1325\nL311@P7: notes, was $747.5 million and a net leverage ratio of 1.6 times adjusted EBITDA.\nL312@P7: The company generated $13 million of positive operating cash flow in the first quarter, despite making strategic\nL313@P7: working capital investments primarily from higher unbilled receivables and inventory. The increase in inventory is\nL315@P7: secure. As expected, free cash flow was negative $36 million in quarter one, reflecting higher capital investments\nL316@P7: to support the expansion of our production facilities. We are still targeting fiscal year 2027 to be negative from a\nL317@P7: free cash flow perspective driven by the increased capital expenditures.\nL318@P7: Now, turning to backlog. Funded backlog totaled $1.5 billion at quarter end, which is 37% higher than the first\nL319@P7: quarter of fiscal year 2026. Funded backlog composition by segment is $1.1 billion or 75% attributable to the AxS\nL320@P7: segment and $358 million or 25% for SCDE segment. Unfunded backlog at the end of the first quarter was $1.4\nL321@P7-8: billion, with $1.2 billion or 89% attributable to the SCDE segment and $157 million or 11% to the AxS segment.AeroVironment, Inc. (AVAV)\nL322@P8: Q1 2027 Earnings Call\nL323@P8: Corrected Transcript\nL324@P8: 09-Sep-2026\nL325@P8: 1-877-FACTSET www.callstreet.com\nL326@P8: 9\nL327@P8: Copyright © 2001-2026 FactSet CallStreet, LLC\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nApplied Digital Reports Fiscal First Quarter 2027 Results :: Applied Digital Corporation (APLD) (https://ir.applieddigital.com/news-events/press-releases/detail/163/applied-digital-reports-fiscal-first-quarter-2027-results)\nciteturn392view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn385view4\",\"pattern\":\"58.8\"}); Total lines: 429\nL50:   * Revenues: $341.9 million, up 322% from the prior year comparable period\nL51:   * Net loss attributable to common stockholders: $221.0 million\nL52:   * Net loss attributable to common stockholders per basic and diluted share: $0.76\nL53:   * Adjusted revenue: $300.4 million\nL54:   * Adjusted net loss: $4.1 million\nL55:   * Adjusted net loss per diluted share: $0.01\nL56:   * Adjusted EBITDA: $64.4 million\nL57:   * Net Operating Income: $58.8 million\nL58: Adjusted revenue, Adjusted net income (loss), Adjusted net income (loss) per diluted share, Adjusted EBITDA, and Net Operating Income are non-GAAP measures. A reconciliation of each of these Non-GAAP Measures to the most directly comparable financial measure presented in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States (“GAAP”) is set forth below. These non-GAAP measures exclude the results of ChronoScale. See “Reconciliation of GAAP to Non-GAAP Measures.”\nL59: \nL60: Recent Highlights\nL104: Services cost of revenues increased $186.9 million, or 318%, from $58.8 million for the three months ended August 31, 2025 to $245.7 million for the three months ended August 31, 2026. The increase in services cost of revenues was primarily due to an increase ofapproximately $151.1 million in expenses associated with tenant fit-out services for our HPC Hosting Business, as well as approximately $22.4 million associated with GPU hardware sales related to ChronoScale.\nL105: Data center rental and other cost of revenues for the three months ended August 31, 2026 were $43.9 million. The primary components included $22.4 million in depreciation and amortization expense on our operational AI Factories at our Polaris Forge 1 campus, $13.3 million in expenses which are reimbursable as tenant recoveries, and $7.8 million in personnel and other operating costs supporting our facilities.\nL116: Adjusted revenue, a non-GAAP financial measure, was $300.4 million for the fiscal first quarter 2027 compared to $64.2 million for the fiscal first quarter of 2026.\nL117: \nL118: Adjusted net loss, a non-GAAP financial measure, was $4.1 million, or $0.01 per diluted share for the fiscal first quarter 2027. This compares to an adjusted net loss, a non-GAAP financial measure, of $7.6 million, or $0.03 per diluted share, for the fiscal first quarter of 2026.\nL119: Adjusted EBITDA, a non-GAAP financial measure, was $64.4 million for the fiscal first quarter 2027 compared to an Adjusted EBITDA of $0.5 million for the fiscal first quarter 2026.\nL120: \nL121: Net Operating Income, a non-GAAP financial measure, was $58.8 million for the fiscal first quarter 2027.\nL122: \nL123: For the details of how the Company defines these non-GAAP financial measures and the reconciliation thereof, please see \"Reconciliation of GAAP to Non-GAAP Measures\" below.\nL124: \nL125: Balance Sheet\nL126: As of August 31, 2026, the Company had $3.7 billion in cash, cash equivalents, and restricted cash, along with $6.4 billion in debt.\nL127: \nL128: Conference Call\nL129: \nL130: As previously announced, Applied Digital will host a conference call today, October 7, 2026, at 5:00 p.m. Eastern Time (2:00 p.m. Pacific Time) to discuss these results. A question-and-answer session will follow the management’s presentation.\nL131: \nL132: Date: Wednesday, October 7, 2026\nL133: \nL134: Time: 5:00 p.m. Eastern Time (2:00 p.m. Pacific Time)\nL135: North America Dial-In: 1-833-461-5787\nL136: \nL137: International Dial-In: +1 (585) 542-9983\nL138: \nL139: Conference ID: 153 131 451\nL140: \nL141: The conference call will be broadcast live and available for replay for one year cite33†here†www.globenewswire.com .\n--------------